    {
        "id": "94",
        "original": "02 · Managed application platform",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "95",
        "original": "A good fit",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "96",
        "original": "Products driven by users and real-time activity",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "97",
        "original": "Marketplaces, social feeds, messaging, booking flows and startup MVPs can benefit from managed authentication, document data, storage and real-time updates.",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "98",
        "original": "Usage-based infrastructure with no-cost allowances",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "99",
        "original": "No server fleet to manage during early validation",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "100",
        "original": "A clear path from prototype to high traffic",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "101",
        "original": "Not our default",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "102",
        "original": "Systems built around complex relational data",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "103",
        "original": "Accounting software, inventory-heavy commerce and reporting systems often need transactions, joins and relational constraints at the centre of the design.",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "104",
        "original": "Read patterns can make document billing unpredictable",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "105",
        "original": "Denormalised models add application complexity",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "106",
        "original": "PostgreSQL or a hybrid architecture may be clearer",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "107",
        "original": "The important distinction:",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "108",
        "original": "Cloud Firestore is a NoSQL document database. Firebase also offers a managed PostgreSQL path, so we choose the data layer—not just the brand name.",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "109",
        "original": "How we work with Firebase →",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
