    },
    {
        "id": "112",
        "original": "Managed AI or specialised inference",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "113",
        "original": "Google \/ AWS",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "114",
        "original": "Integrated enterprise AI platforms",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "115",
        "original": "Google Cloud and AWS combine models with identity, storage, monitoring, governance and other cloud services. That integration is useful when those controls are part of the requirement.",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "116",
        "original": "Centralised access and cloud governance",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "117",
        "original": "Integration with existing cloud data",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "118",
        "original": "Broad managed-service ecosystem",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "119",
        "original": "Groq \/ Fireworks",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "120",
        "original": "Focused model inference APIs",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "121",
        "original": "Specialised providers can offer a smaller integration surface and additional choices for open models, latency and inference pricing when a complete enterprise platform is unnecessary.",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "122",
        "original": "Direct, API-focused implementation",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "123",
        "original": "Choice of supported open models",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "124",
        "original": "Costs measured against the actual workload",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "125",
        "original": "The model is only one component:",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "126",
        "original": "retrieval, permissions, evaluation, logging and fallback behaviour still need to be designed in the application.",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
