        "id": "129",
        "original": "04 · Hosting infrastructure",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "130",
        "original": "Cloud fits",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "131",
        "original": "Applications with changing requirements",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "132",
        "original": "Cloud platforms provide managed databases, object storage, queues, private networks, monitoring and capacity that can be changed without replacing the entire hosting environment.",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "133",
        "original": "Scale individual components independently",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "134",
        "original": "Managed backups, regions and access controls",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "135",
        "original": "Infrastructure can be described and reproduced",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "136",
        "original": "Classic hosting fits",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "137",
        "original": "Small and predictable workloads",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "138",
        "original": "A conventional server or hosting plan can be simpler and cheaper for a stable website or application that does not need several managed services or rapid changes in capacity.",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "139",
        "original": "Predictable monthly cost",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "140",
        "original": "Less infrastructure to configure",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "141",
        "original": "A better fit when scaling needs are modest",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "142",
        "original": "Cloud is not automatically cheaper:",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "143",
        "original": "its advantage is service choice, automation and scaling. Costs still require monitoring and architecture limits.",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
    },
    {
        "id": "144",
        "original": "How we use cloud infrastructure →",
        "translated": "",
        "status": "0"
